Let's look directly at the requirement in the case study:&quot;The product sheets must be processed by using an indexing pipeline that enables semantic and vector search, so that Agent1 can retrieve the relevant product information.
In Azure AI Search / Foundry indexing pipelines, generating vector embeddings from unstructured text documents (like the product sheets in storage1) requires two fundamental, coupled built-in skills:
(1)Text Split (#Microsoft.Skills.Text.SplitSkill):Documents like product detail sheets in PDF format are typically multi-page and exceed model token limits.Before text can be vectorized, it must be chunked into semantically meaningful segments (pages, paragraphs, or fixed token lengths).
(2)Azure OpenAI Embedding (#Microsoft.Skills.Text.AzureOpenAIEmbeddingSkill):Takes the individual text chunks output by the Text Split skill and generates the high-dimensional numerical vectors (embeddings) needed to populate the search index.This is what directly enables vector search.Together, Text Split then Azure OpenAI Embedding is the standard, foundational enrichment pipeline for vector search indexing in Azure.
The word &quot;embedding&quot; comes directly from mathematics (topology and geometry): discrete, symbolic human language is being embedded into a continuous, geometric vector space.
{&quot;dog&quot;} = [1, 0, 0, 0}
{&quot;cat&quot;} = [0, 1, 0, 0}
{&quot;apple&quot;} = [0, 0, 1, 0}

